# Expected sha256 of the VENDORED STYLE BLOCK in
# defaults/templates/artifact-outcome.html — the lines strictly between the
# `<style>` and `</style>` lines, hashed exactly as they appear.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS, IN THE TEST TREE AND NOT IN THE TEMPLATE.
# The template already carries a `sha256:` line in its own header, and
# test-aid-artifact-render.bats used to check the CSS against that line alone.
# Both values live in the same file, so editing the CSS and its header hash
# together passed — the "guard" was a file agreeing with itself, which every
# file does. The digest below is a SECOND, INDEPENDENTLY OWNED copy: a restyle
# of the vendored block now has to be recorded here as well, in a different
# tree, as a deliberate and reviewable act. That is the whole mechanism; it is
# not cryptography, it is a second signature.
#
# Verified byte-identical against the upstream _CSS in
# /opt/eco/projects/agents/agent-report.py on 2026-08-12.
#
# TO UPDATE: re-vendor the CSS, then run
#   sed -n '/^<style>$/,/^<\/style>$/p' \
#     plugins/aid-orchestrator/defaults/templates/artifact-outcome.html \
#     | sed '1d;$d' | sha256sum
# and paste the digest below, replacing the old one.
fb48aa62b99ba7db4d36326876683584873c576005b34b0aad5492587be501b6
